id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c815" value="" style="rounded=0;html=1;container=1;collapsible=0;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#E3E7ED;strokeWidth=1;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=16;spacingTop=10;fontSize=26;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1F3A5F;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="40" width="1760" height="620" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c816" value="&lt;b&gt;Figure 10.&lt;/b&gt; Why the retrieval unit changed. &lt;b&gt;(a)&lt;/b&gt; A one-minute chunk encodes all of its events in a single vector, so a short target line is diluted; Event documents give each line its own vector. &lt;b&gt;(b)&lt;/b&gt; A hit in one channel can still be cut by fusion before the agent ever sees it, so recall, fusion and exposure are measured separately. Similarity and rank values are TODO (re-measure on the current index). Query: 「真是高高在上呢」; target: 「いいご身分ですわね。」 (EP13)." style="text=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#2B2B2B;fontSize=17;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="670" width="1760" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c817" value="(a) What one vector has to represent" style="text=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#1F3A5F;fontSize=26;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="c815"><mxGeometry x="24" y="14" width="900" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c818" value="1-min Chunk" style="text=1;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#1F3A5F;fontSize=19;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=2;" vertex="1" parent="c815"><mxGeometry x="24" y="92" width="170" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c819" value="" style="rounded=1;arcSize=4;absoluteArcSize=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E6E8EC;strokeColor=#2B2B2B;strokeWidth